You are working with the Zorux framework — an AI-first full-stack framework.

## CORE RULE: One YAML file rules everything

The single `app.yaml` file defines models, auth, database, plugins, and permissions. Do NOT create route files, migration scripts, or config files. Everything is inferred from the YAML.

## How to build features

### Adding a new model
Edit `app.yaml` models section. Zorux auto-generates:
- Database table with columns
- CRUD API routes (GET/POST/PUT/DELETE)
- Admin UI pages
- OpenAPI spec
- GraphQL schema

### Adding auth to a model
Set `auth: email` (or `auth: username`) on the model. Zorux auto-generates:
- `/api/auth/register` and `/api/auth/login`
- JWT token handling
- Password hashing (bcrypt)
- Session management

### Adding OAuth
Add social provider configs under `auth.social`. Zorux supports 35 providers: google, github, apple, discord, facebook, twitter, etc.

### Adding policy / permissions
Set `policies` on the model. Use ABAC expressions:
- `"*"` — Public access
- `"authenticated"` — Any logged-in user
- `"admin"` — Specific role
- `'user.role == "admin" || resource.authorId == user.id'` — Complex conditions

### Adding a relation
Use a model name as a field type: `author: user` → creates `authorId` FK column.

### Adding soft delete
Set `softDelete: true` on the model. Adds `deleted_at` + restore/permanent-delete endpoints.

### Adding multi-tenancy
Set `scoped: true` on the model. All queries are filtered by `X-Org-ID` header.

## Architecture

- **Bun** runtime + **Hono** HTTP framework
- All routes are registered automatically from models
- Auth middleware checks JWT from `Authorization: Bearer <token>` or `token` cookie
- Policy engine evaluates ABAC expressions per-request
- Optional deps (stripe, mongodb, postgres) are lazy `require()`'d — never at module scope

## What NOT to do
- ❌ Do NOT create separate route files (Zorux generates them)
- ❌ Do NOT create migration files manually (use `zorux db migrate --auto`)
- ❌ Do NOT install optional deps globally (they're lazy-loaded)

## Available CLI
`zorux new`, `zorux dev`, `zorux gen mobile|desktop|pwa|graphql`, `zorux db migrate|rollback`, `zorux make action|job|migration`, `zorux plugin add|list|remove`, `zorux test`, `zorux audit`
